ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: stacks.seq.stack
display_id: SEQ-STACKS-MANAGE
module: stacks
title: List, create, rename, or delete a stack
summary: Lets the owner manage stacks by name; deleting one hands off to complete deletion after an interactive
  confirmation.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: user
  text: The owner runs a stack command, or a script calls the stack method
operation: stacks.op.stack
participants:
- actor.owner
- sys.cli
- sys.daemon
- id: registry
  is:
  - sys.home
  label: Stack registry
items:
- msg:
    from: actor.owner
    to: sys.cli
    text: Manage stacks
    owner: crates/kernle-cli/src/commands/stack.rs::run
- alt:
    branches:
    - when: listing
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.cli
          to: registry
          text: Read every stack with its kind, identity, size, last activity, and sync state
          ops:
          - op: read
            entity: stacks.data.stack
            by:
            - every row
    - when: creating a named stack
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.cli
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Register the named stack and create its directory and database
          guards:
          - the name is a valid slug and not already taken
          ops:
          - op: insert
            entity: stacks.data.stack
            index: U1
            set:
            - stack_id the name
            - kind named
            - root_key named and the name
            - created_at now
          results:
          - code: stack_exists
            when: the name is taken
            copy: A stack with that name already exists.
    - when: renaming
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.cli
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Change the stack's display name
          ops:
          - op: update
            entity: stacks.data.stack
            by:
            - stack_id
            set:
            - display_name
    - when: deleting
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.cli
          to: actor.owner
          text: Show what the stack holds and ask for the stack's name to confirm
          guards:
          - standard input and output are an interactive terminal
          results:
          - code: needs_terminal
            when: not an interactive terminal
            copy: Deleting a stack needs an interactive terminal. Nothing was deleted.
      - msg:
          from: sys.cli
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Delete the stack completely
          invokes:
          - retention.seq.stack-delete
rationale: Deleting a stack requires typing its name in an interactive terminal, because agents run under
  the owner's account and their tool shells are not interactive, so no agent can delete a whole stack
  on its own.
